// Pressure-driven model-full steady BVP: fixed-pressure boundaries on both
// ends of a vertical incompressible riser running the full gas momentum
// closure (distributed pressure momentum). Neither phase rate is prescribed
// - the drive 2e5 Pa accelerates the column through the mixture-row Newton
// (implicit Euler, holdup frozen) and the rates EMERGE at the boundaries.
//
// The slip ODE (mixture pressure gradient substituted, convective gas term
// active in the transient) settles on the buoyancy/drag terminal
//   s* = sqrt(alpha_g alpha (rhoL - rhoG) g sinT / C)  (C = 800, sinT = 1)
// which is rhoG-independent. The semi-implicit origin-secant drag needs
// |s_old| > 0 to engage, so the first step overshoots to
// s1 = (rhoL - rhoG) g dt / rhoG; rhoG = 300 and dt = 0.05 keep that
// overshoot below s*(0.8) = 1.31 for a smooth start-up (the fullmomentum
// case made the ODE genuinely inertial the same way).
//
// The ghost composition IS the steady holdup: at the uniform fixed point
// the face-0 flux upwinds from the ghost, so the pipe relaxes to
// alpha* = alpha_ghost = 0.5 (the alternative flux root a' = 1 - vm/s -
// alpha needs vm < s; here vm* ~ 4.9 > s* ~ 1.46, so the root is unique).
// vM* solves the steady row  dpDrive = sum(churchill fr + gravity head)
// with the homogeneous mixture properties at alpha* = 0.5
// (rho_m = 650, mu_m = 0.005005), giving vM* ~ 4.92 m/s, s* = 1.464652,
// and the emergent inlet rates vL = F(0.5, s*) ~ 2.09, vG = G(0.5, s*) ~ 2.83.
// At the settled state the loss march from the inlet anchor lands exactly
// on the outlet pressure: p[node N] = p_in - sum loss = p_out.
//
// tests/check_two_fluid.py mode pressurefull replicates the coupled
// momentum-Newton + slip + Godunov-water recursion step by step (1e-9),
// then checks the steady anchors above and the transient convective
// diagnostic. Initial alpha 0.8 / water 0.5 deliberately differ from the
// fixed point so the flush to (0.5, 0.25) is a real transient.
fluid
{
    rhoL 1000;
    rhoG 300;
    muL  0.01;
    muG  1e-5;
}

pipe
{
    length 20;
    diameter 0.05;
    roughness 0;
    angleDeg 90;
    sections 20;
}

closure
{
    model full;
    interfacialDrag 800;
}

initial
{
    alpha 0.8;
    water 0.5;
}

boundaries
{
    inlet  { type fixedPressure; p 3.0e5; alpha 0.5; waterFraction 0.25; }
    outlet { type fixedPressure; p 1.0e5; }
}

time
{
    dt 0.05;
    endTime 30;
    reportEvery 20;
}
